# trx64g.cor (T104.2 Q5): the same monolith bitstream with Gideon's Ultimate application, both taken from the TRX64-Ultimate CI package
# trx64-ultimate/<PKG_VERSION> (read only). APP_FILE is the .app (12-byte record header + image); the packer strips it and refuses a file whose
# SHA-256 is not APP_SHA256.
# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
# PROVENANCE: copied from TRX64U-MultiCore, branch t239.3, commit cfa7872a, release/imports/trx64g.pin (GPL-3.0-or-later, MultiCore's LICENSING.md), for
# MultiCore T239.3 D46. Changed here, the pin values: MultiCore's pin named one reviewed package version (main-d94aa68e, release 0.3.1); this one packs
# the package of each CI run, so VERSION, SEMVER, PKG_VERSION, BIT_SHA256 and APP_SHA256 are empty here and ci/cor.sh appends the run's values to its
# copy (the package's <commit8>, the manifest's "version", <branch>-<commit8>, the manifest's sha256 of c64_basic.bit and of ultimate.app). ICON is
# this folder's copy of MultiCore's tools/core_logos/trx64/icon.rgb565. No DESC, OPS, FILES or HEAP, as in MultiCore's pin: trx64g.cor holds of the
# Commodore ROMs only what the application holds (README.md).
ID=trx64g
NAME="TRX64 Ultimate (Gideon app)"
VERSION=
SEMVER=
PKG_VERSION=
BIT_FILE=c64_basic.bit
BIT_SHA256=
APP_FILE=ultimate.app
APP_SHA256=
ICON=icon.rgb565
